  "body": "The first landed maintenance diagnostic stopped in its pure Python checks before any Go build or benchmark. Python 3.12 adds `FunctionDef.type_params` to `ast.dump`, so the unchanged collector failed hashes produced with Python 3.10 ([failed run](https://github.com/snissn/gomap/actions/runs/38830037922)).\n\nBind the three reviewed functions to their exact source bytes instead. Their source still matches the original reviewed collector; the fixed inputs, fourteen-call schedule, parser, limits and workflow are unchanged.\n\nValidation: all 10 pure controls pass on Python 3.9.23 and 3.10.12; emulating Python 3.12's added AST field reproduces the exact hosted mismatch. `git diff --check` passes. Independent exact gpt-6.1-sol review ACCEPT is complete; required current-head CI is running. No Go build, benchmark or diagnostic redispatch is part of this PR.\n\nRelated to #4871 and follow-up to #5137.\n\n\n[Retained failed attempt, verified original artifact, exact source repair and independent review](https://github.com/snissn/gomap/tree/3c20504a46de42da8450ed10dd05d72b0ec57dd2/artifacts/4871/20261016-host185-maintenance-portability). Internal independent review is used because the hosted trigger cannot pin the required exact model. The original failed attempt remains retained; no diagnostic redispatch has occurred.\n",
